{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And He brought him outside.</b> It is not the way of the world to see the stars from inside the house until one goes outside the house, and he used this expression regarding Abraham because until now he prophesied from within the degree called Bet El (בית אל), which David, of blessed memory, called (Psalms 45) ״כבודה בת מלך פנימה״; therefore he needed to use now the expression 'and He brought him out.' And the opinion of our Rabbis, of blessed memory, is that He brought him outside the constellation-formation, and so they expounded: 'ויוצא אותו החוצה' — He said to him: 'Go out of your astrology.' 'Look now toward the heavens' — the expression הבטה (looking) is only from above downward, in the manner of what is written (Psalms 80) ״הבט משמים וראה״, and it is written (Psalms 102) ״ה' משמים אל ארץ הביט״; and our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded that He lifted him above the stars and the constellations, and the stars and constellations were like a stepping-stone beneath his foot." "<b>And according to</b> my opinion, this is the meaning of (Isaiah 41:2) ״צדק יקראהו לרגלו״ — concerning the star צדק (Jupiter); and from here our Sages, of blessed memory, proved that 'there is no constellation for Israel,' for they are above them. And so they said in the Midrash on (Song of Songs 8:14) ״ברח דודי ודמה לך לצבי״ — this is Abraham, who was called 'my beloved.' ״על הרי בשמים״ — do not read בשמים but בשמים (in the heavens). And they said: 'There is no constellation for Israel' — the meaning of this applies to the totality of Israel, but in their individual capacity each and every one does have a constellation, for the wisdom of the constellations is a great and glorious wisdom, and our Rabbis, of blessed memory, do not deny it at all." "<b>And count the stars, if you are able to count them.</b> That is: 'And count the stars, if you can count them' — so shall your seed be, in a vast multitude like these stars which are uncountable for their abundance.'" "And <b>so shall your seed be</b> further includes the degrees of wisdom: for just as among the stars there are those whose light is more radiant and brilliant than that of another, and their degrees are differentiated, one above another, in illumination and in apprehension, so too will the sages of Israel in the future have differentiated degrees — the light of this one's Torah above the light of that one's Torah, and this one's apprehension above that one's apprehension." "And <b>so shall your seed be</b> further includes the degrees of reward and eternal pleasure in the World to Come, for there is reward for the souls that attain differentiated degrees, one above another, and a canopy above a canopy, and light above light; and so our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded in the Sifre: 'For seven joys, the faces of the righteous are destined to resemble (in the world to come): to the sun, to the moon, to the firmament, to the stars, to the lightnings, to the lilies, to the lamp of the Temple.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {1 "The wordplay אל תקרי בשמים אלא בשמים is between two vocalizations of the same consonants; both are rendered identically in transliteration as the text does not specify the alternative vocalization."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:36.674200467Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}